WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.040
As relative sea level rises, marine environments shift over

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:06.080
former coastal and land settings. Watch the shoreline move

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:10.340
landward: transgression. Subsidence can contribute without a global rise

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:13.500
in sea level. Now the shoreline moves seaward. Coastal

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:18.340
sediment can overlie former offshore deposits. Regression and progradation

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:21.720
reflect the balance between water level, available space, and

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:25.260
sediment supply. Erosion removes part of the record before

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:30.400
deposition resumes. Textures, fossils, and structures help reconstruct the

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:34.380
history. A porous reservoir beneath an impermeable seal can

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:38.480
trap migrated petroleum. Reservoir rock alone does not prove

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:39.520
a usable resource.
